# Agent instructions for {{LibraryName}}

This file is the canonical source of instructions for AI coding agents
working in this repo (Claude, Copilot, etc). `CLAUDE.md` is a thin pointer
to this file -- update conventions here, not there.

## Repo shape

`src/` holds the library, its unit tests, and benchmarks. `smoketests/`
validates the published package. `docs/design/` holds maintainer-facing
design docs (PRD, ADRs). See `docs/design/adr/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md`
for why the repo is laid out this way.

## Conventions

- Public API surface is the product -- treat every public member as a
  compatibility commitment. Prefer `internal` until an API is proven out.
- Partial-class files segregate interface implementations, e.g.
  `Type.cs`, `Type.Factory.cs`, `Type.IComparable.cs`, `Type.Operators.cs`.
  Follow this pattern for new types rather than one large file.
- No logical-layer folders inside the library (no `Services/`, `Models/`,
  `Core/`). Sub-directories are for cross-cutting concerns only.
- Unit tests mirror the library 1:1 -- a test for `Foo.cs` lives in a test
  file with a matching name, so either side can be found from the other.

## Build & verify

```bash
cd src && dotnet build && dotnet test
```

Run this before considering a change complete. CI also runs CodeQL and a
smoke test against the packed `.nupkg` -- a change can pass unit tests and
still fail packaging, so don't skip the smoke test step for changes that
touch `.csproj` files or public API shape.

## Things not to do

- Don't hand-edit `.slnx` files -- use `dotnet sln add/remove`.
- Don't hand-edit `packages.lock.json` -- regenerate via
  `dotnet restore --use-lock-file`.
- Don't add new top-level folders without updating
  `docs/design/adr/` to record why.
